# Feedback & Suggestions page (src/app/feedback) — this is a fully static
# site with no backend, so form submissions go straight to Web3Forms
# (https://web3forms.com), which forwards them to Morshed's email.
#
# To get a real key: go to https://web3forms.com/create-api-key, enter
# morshedux@gmail.com, and the access key arrives by email instantly — no
# account/password needed. Copy it into a local .env.local (never commit
# that file — .gitignore already excludes .env* except this example).
#
# This key is meant to be public (it's used directly in client-side
# fetch() calls) — Web3Forms' spam/domain controls live on their
# dashboard, not in the key itself. It is NOT a secret like an API
# password would be.
NEXT_PUBLIC_WEB3FORMS_KEY=
